## 3. Impact Assessment & Required Changes

| # | Component / Object | Object Type | Current Behavior | Required Modification |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **1** | **External Data Script** | SQL / Batch Script | Populates `WP Customer Roles Audit` / triggers the workflow for `LIVE` merchants only. | Update the script's filtering criteria (`WHERE` clause) to include `CLOSED`, `SUSPENDED`, and other target trading statuses. |
| **2** | **`WP Kafka Send Trading Status Datafix Update`** (Step: `Check Rule Live?` -> Branch: `Live`) | Workflow Process (Siebel Tools) | Condition checks `RoleStatus` with operation `All Must Match (Ignore Case)` = `LIVE`. | 1. Change **Operation** from `All Must Match (Ignore Case)` to **`One Must Match (Ignore Case)`**.<br>2. Add target status LIC values (`CLOSED`, `SUSPENDED`, etc.) to the **Values** list alongside `LIVE`. |
| **3** | **`WP Kafka Send Trading Status Datafix Update`** (Step: `Check Roles`) | Workflow Process (Siebel Tools) | Queries `WP EAI Customer Roles` with `([Valid To] IS NULL OR [Valid To] >= Today())`. | **Conditional (Pending Confirmation):** If `CLOSED` merchants have a past `Valid To` date on their Trading Status record, remove or adjust the `Valid To` condition in the `Search Spec` so closed records are not filtered out. |
| **4** | **Rule 0 (`Publish Customer Role Change Message Data Script`)** & **IO (`WP MF Get PO Config IO`)** | Data Config / Siebel Tools | Uses `EventName = MerchantPromotedEventDbScript` and extracts all `Customer Roles` without status filtering. | **No changes required** (assuming downstream consumers accept the same `EventName` for all trading status updates). |

